Mechanism:
- main.rs:78 — FocusState owns the UI Stage, input timing and deferred Locate.
  Snapshot reconciliation preserves surviving local focus; new membership can
  select the new pane. Explicit focus calls the accepted Focus core on a scratch
  UI model only for the input action; an ordinary publication/frame clones no scratch UI model.
- main.rs:199 — real winit and synthetic tests share route_key. Terminal plain
  Tab/arrows/text/control/Alt use the unchanged terminal_input encoder. Cmd+Opt
  arrows/Tab use the pure pane navigation. Launcher keys are local; repeats move
  selection but never repeat a pick, Escape or the global open/quit/HUD action.
- main.rs:307/451/536 — catalog records use stable ids and D1c's provider projection;
  open hosts the existing Launcher/Controller. The default plain root zsh pick
  uses the existing bounded SpawnZsh. Other ids/modifier placements log the named
  not_wired_yet outcome. Query text and IME commits are local; caret, selection
  and preedit are explicitly a checkpoint C gap. Non-zsh dispatch is checkpoint B.
- main.rs:584 — pane click and explicit keyboard navigation update Stage through
  Focus; Scene no longer mutates focus independently. Watched ordering, generation
  checks, admission and terminal body sizes keep the existing IO path.
- scene.rs:237/333 — Scene projects the supplied Stage; spatial hit/navigation
  rects are the outer panes, independent of terminal body sizing.
- scene.rs:545/594 — the full-window Overlay and existing Launcher compose the
  foreground. It retains its exact painted panel/query/row rects for input.
  Live cells precede unwrapped launcher ops; HUD follows last. The frozen path
  uses the same order. No renderer, gpu.rs, provider model or live.rs edits.
- main.rs --launcher — debug/verification-only startup flag, same controller;
  enables IME when the owned native window is created. Listed under Debug in help.

