No-menu baseline replay harness (the accepted source needs only this test append):
#[cfg(test)]
mod l8_baseline_probe {
    #[test]
    fn no_launcher_paint_proof() {
        let scene = super::Scene::new();
        let size = [1600., 960.];
        let layouts = scene.layout(size, false).unwrap();
        let paints = scene.paint(&layouts, size, None);
        println!("L8_PAINT_BEGIN{paints:#?}L8_PAINT_END");
        assert_eq!(scene.pane_bounds(&layouts).len(), 15);
    }
}
Run on base 4bb0417 with its own detached worktree and own CARGO_TARGET_DIR:
cargo test -p bboxy450-term --bin bboxy450-term --locked
no_launcher_paint_proof -- --nocapture
Final source carries scene::launcher_tests::no_launcher_paint_proof, which calls
paint(..., None, None). Extract bytes strictly between the same markers and
compare with ==; sha256 is recorded above for identification. The probe uses
only font shaping and painting; it starts no custody or processes.

